\label{fig:calibration}
\end{figure}

\subsection{Sensor-only deployment}

Two NEWS2 parameters, supplemental oxygen and consciousness, are recorded by
staff rather than sensed. A deployment fed only by wearables cannot supply them,
and the interface defaults them to the benign case. This is failure mode F5, and
it is silent in the same way F3 is: nothing errors, the numbers simply get
worse.

Table~\ref{tab:wearable} and Fig.~\ref{fig:wearable} quantify it. Serving the
fully-trained model on a sensor-only feed raises the missed-HIGH rate more than
three-fold. Retraining for the inputs actually present recovers most of the
safety margin while barely changing macro-F1---another instance of the aggregate
metric concealing the clinically relevant difference.

